<!-- YouTube app (resources/lib/youtube_app.py), laid out like YouTube on a TV: a black page (#0F0F0F), the section rail on
     the left, rounded 16:9 thumbnails with the title in two lines and one grey line under each, no boxes.
     Controls: 100 section rail, 150 the button over the account's circle (OK: the "Who's watching" picker), 200 video grid,
     300 the card's button, 401-404 what a search is for (Videos, Channels, Playlists, Live).
     Window properties: mode (data | signin | needkey | empty | loading | error | unavailable | prompt), demo, signed (1 | 0 | none),
     search (1 while the search is shown: the row 401-404 is), kind (video | channel | playlist | live: the chosen one),
     splash (1 while the launch splash is up: every other control is hidden; none: the screen; the splash is also shown
     while mode is still empty, the instant the window is built and Python has decided nothing, so that no frame of a
     half-empty card is drawn), avatar (the letter in the circle, none: no circle), avatar_color, title (the section's name), notice (the line
     at the bottom while the next page loads), msg_title, msg_text, action (the button's label; none: no button).
     The "Set up your Google key" card (mode needkey) also reads key_qr (the phone page's QR picture, none: no QR),
     key_url (its address), step ("Step 2 of 6: <title>"), step_hint1, step_hint2 (the hint in two lines); step is
     none when no wizard runs on the phone (they are cut to their labels in Python, see youtube_cards.step_lines).
     List item properties of the grid: title1, title2 (the title cut into its two lines, an ellipsis at the end of a
     long one), meta (the channel), meta2 ("1.2M views · 3 days ago"; both are filled from the top), badge (the text in the pill on the picture: length, LIVE, 24 videos), strip
     (the name of the one picture that holds the pill and the watched bar; none: neither), kind (video | folder); art
     "thumb" the picture. The rail's items have the properties active and icon.
     Rules the tests hold this file to:
     - every label of a list layout sets <selectedcolor> as well as <textcolor>: a selected item takes that colour;
     - the thumbnail is rounded by a diffuse mask (youtube-mask.png, as the launcher's cards are), no box behind it;
     - a card's title is two labels cut in Python (a label that is too wide scrolls sideways when focused);
     - 9-slice textures (border=) are at least twice the border in each direction, and so is the control they fill;
     - every top-level control but the splash group has a visible condition with `splash` empty and `mode` set in it, and
       the splash group shows exactly when `splash` is set or `mode` is empty (one picture, no control to focus: Back
       leaves the app);
     - Budget (Pi 3B+): at most 34 pictures in view at once (counted by the test: 4 x 2 cards and the top of a third row
       with one thumbnail and one strip each, ring, avatar, logo, rail), no animation, thumbnails load in the background.
     The grid is 4 columns of 384 (352 picture + 32 gap) and rows of 382: two rows and the top 144 px of a third. -->
